{
 "description": "Pair alarms read from a backup (Android AlarmJson.fromJson / iOS BackupManager.alarmFromJson). An unknown condition (newer app version) or a threshold that is not a finite number makes the alarm invalid: it is counted and named in the restore confirmation, never turned into «price above» with a foreign threshold. Numbers JSON cannot hold are strings (\"NaN\"). An optional \"windowHours\" per case is the expected window after reading: clamped to 1 … 365 (no overflow, no 32-bit wrap). A threshold <= 0 is also invalid for price level (PRICE_ABOVE/BELOW), percent change (CHANGE_PERCENT_UP/DOWN) and move (MOVE_PERCENT_WINDOW) alarms — they fired on every check; funding may be negative and «near high/low» may be 0. A falling percent alarm (CHANGE_PERCENT_DOWN, OI_DOWN) with a threshold >= 100 is invalid as well — a drop of 100 % or more never fires; rising and move alarms stay open. Such a falling alarm >= 100 % is no longer invalid: it is taken over but switched off (the alarm list marks it «threshold invalid – please adjust»). An optional \"expectedEnabled\" per case is the enabled state after reading.",
